        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Nice! Is there a way to remove item from the list as well?\r\n\r\nNot the easy one, no. You can restart `builtin.buffers()` after deleting, but this might lead to some flicker. You can also get all items prior to wipe out (`MiniPick.get_picker_items()`), wipe out and modify the array accordingly, and then set it back (`MiniPick.set_picker_items()`). Either way, this is out of scope for `builtin.buffers()` and 'mini.pick' in general as it is more focused on picking and not manipulating.",
            "created_at": "2023-10-18T07:00:00Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/525#issuecomment-1767795741",
